---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { checkerUrl, sitePath } from '../lib/urls';
---

<Page
  title="Instagram follow-back checker for uploaded files"
  description="Upload Instagram JSON, HTML or ZIP files to see who does not follow you back. Compare locally with searchable results and scope-aware exports."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR CONNECTIONS, WITH CONTEXT</p><h1>
        A clearer view of{' '}<br />who follows you back.
      </h1><p class="hero-description">
        Upload your Instagram files. See who appears in following but not
        followers, then search, browse and export the results.
      </p><div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={checkerUrl('import')}
          >Upload your Instagram files <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        ><a class="secondary-link" href={checkerUrl('automatic')}
          >Automatic checking</a
        >
      </div><p class="availability">
        <span aria-hidden="true">○</span> Automatic checking is currently unavailable.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="connection-card" aria-label="How your connections are compared">
      <div class="connection-top">TWO LISTS. THREE USEFUL GROUPS.</div>
      <div class="connection-title">The overlap, made clear.</div>
      <div class="connection-groups">
        <div class="connection-group highlighted">
          <span class="relation-symbol" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Not following you back</strong><p>
              In following, absent from followers.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="connection-group">
          <span class="relation-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↔</span>
          <div><strong>Mutual followers</strong><p>In both your lists.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="connection-group">
          <span class="relation-symbol" aria-hidden="true">←</span>
          <div>
            <strong>You don’t follow back</strong><p>
              In followers, absent from following.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="connection-caption">
        Based on your uploaded files. Search every list and download your
        results.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="principles">
    <span><span aria-hidden="true">01</span> Readable lists</span><span
      ><span aria-hidden="true">02</span> Context with every result</span
    ><span><span aria-hidden="true">03</span> An ad-free checker</span>
  </div>
  <section class="section-block explanation">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">TWO LISTS. A BETTER PICTURE.</p><h2>
        Make sense of<br />your connections.
      </h2><p>
        Followers and following describe different directions. A follow-back
        report compares them, without making assumptions about anyone’s reasons.
      </p><a
        class="text-link"
        href={sitePath('/guides/followers-vs-following/')}
        >Understand the three groups <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
      >
    </div><div class="definition-list">
      <article>
        <span class="definition-number">01</span><div>
          <h3>Mutuals</h3><p>
            You follow them, and they appear in your followers list.
          </p>
        </div><span class="relation-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↔</span>
      </article><article>
        <span class="definition-number">02</span><div>
          <h3>Not following you back</h3><p>
            They appear in your uploaded following list but not your followers
            list.
          </p>
        </div><span class="relation-symbol" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </article><article>
        <span class="definition-number">03</span><div>
          <h3>You don’t follow back</h3><p>
            They appear in your uploaded followers list but not your following
            list.
          </p>
        </div><span class="relation-symbol" aria-hidden="true">←</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="integrity-panel">
    <div class="eyebrow">YOUR FILES, YOUR DEVICE</div><h2>
      Your connections stay in your hands.
    </h2><p>
      Your files are read and compared in your browser. No password is needed,
      and nothing is saved unless you choose to save a snapshot or download a
      report. If a file is missing parts, the affected results say so.
    </p><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/privacy/')}
      >How your data is handled <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
    >
  </section>
  <section class="section-block guides-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CONTEXT GOES A LONG WAY</p><h2>
          Read before you interpret.
        </h2>
      </div><span class="muted">Practical guides, without the guesswork.</span>
    </div><div class="guide-grid">
      <a class="guide-card" href={sitePath('/guides/followers-vs-following/')}
        ><span>THE BASICS</span><h3>Followers vs. following</h3><p>
          Two directions, three useful groups. Start with a simple example.
        </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      ><a
        class="guide-card"
        href={sitePath('/guides/not-following-back-vs-unfollowed/')}
        ><span>READING RESULTS</span><h3>
          Not following back isn’t the same as unfollowed
        </h3><p>
          What one report can tell you, and what requires a history.
        </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      ><a
        class="guide-card"
        href={sitePath('/guides/instagram-export-troubleshooting/')}
        ><span>LOCAL IMPORTS</span><h3>When an export looks incomplete</h3><p>
          Missing directions, split files, and source dates explained.
        </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      ><a class="guide-card" href={sitePath('/guides/')}>
        <span>ALL GUIDES</span><h3>Prepare, compare and revisit</h3><p>
          Browse export, terminology, troubleshooting and snapshot guidance.
        </p><span class="guide-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
